.TH elfshaker 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker \- Store and restore deduplicated snapshots of a working directory.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker\fR [GLOBAL\-OPTS] <SUBCOMMAND> [SUBCOMMAND\-OPTS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
elfshaker stores snapshots of the current working directory in a separate data directory. Snapshots may remain loose or be combined into compressed packs.
.PP
Commands that restore files write to the working directory. \-\-data\-dir only selects the data directory.
.SH TERMINOLOGY
.TP
\fBWorking directory\fR
The directory containing the files that elfshaker stores and restores. It is normally the directory from which you run elfshaker.
.TP
\fBData directory\fR
The directory where elfshaker keeps snapshots and its other state, including packs, indexes, loose objects, remotes, and HEAD. It defaults to elfshaker_data and can be selected with \-\-data\-dir.
.TP
\fBRepository\fR
A working directory together with its associated data directory.
.TP
\fBSnapshot\fR
A record of selected files from the working directory at a point in time.
.TP
\fBSnapshot tag\fR
The name of a snapshot. You choose the tag when you store a snapshot and use it later to list, inspect, or restore that snapshot. PACK:SNAPSHOT identifies a snapshot in a specific pack.
.TP
\fBLoose snapshot\fR
A snapshot stored as a loose index and loose objects in the data directory. The store command creates this form. The pack command can combine loose snapshots into a pack.
.TP
\fBPack\fR
A compressed file containing the data used by one or more snapshots. A companion pack index records the snapshots and files available from the pack.
.TP
\fBRemote index (.esi)\fR
A small catalog of packs published by a remote source. It records where each pack can be downloaded and the checksums of the pack and its pack index. The clone and update commands fetch remote indexes and pack indexes. Pack data is downloaded only when needed.
.TP
\fBHEAD\fR
The snapshot elfshaker uses as the starting point for the next incremental extraction. The store and extract commands update HEAD.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Use PATH as the data directory containing packs, indexes, loose objects, remotes, and HEAD. This does not change the working directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
elfshaker\-extract(1)
Restore a snapshot into the working directory.
.TP
elfshaker\-store(1)
Store files from the working directory as a loose snapshot.
.TP
elfshaker\-list(1)
List snapshots in known pack indexes.
.TP
elfshaker\-list\-packs(1)
List pack indexes known to the data directory.
.TP
elfshaker\-list\-files(1)
List files recorded in a snapshot.
.TP
elfshaker\-pack(1)
Combine loose snapshots into a compressed pack.
.TP
elfshaker\-show(1)
Write files from a snapshot to standard output.
.TP
elfshaker\-find(1)
Search snapshot tags in known pack indexes.
.TP
elfshaker\-gc(1)
Delete redundant loose snapshots and unreferenced loose objects.
.TP
elfshaker\-update(1)
Refresh indexes for all configured remotes.
.TP
elfshaker\-clone(1)
Create a working directory configured from a remote index.
.TP
elfshaker\-esi(1)
Creates and edits elfshaker remote indexes
.TP
elfshaker\-explode(1)
Materialize a pack\*(Aqs objects in the loose\-object store.
.SH VERSION
v1.0.0\-rc1
